@* ProjectsPage: the list of projects, at "/projects". Choosing a project is what nearly every visit is for, so the
   list is the whole page. A system administrator sees every project and gets a "+ New project" link to the
   separate creation page at "/projects/new"; everybody else sees only the projects they are a member of, with no
   creation link (only a system administrator may create a project).

   Presentation only; state lives in ProjectsPage.razor.cs. Every interactive element and every key value carries a
   stable kebab-case data-testid (row-level ids carry the project id), and the data-interactive marker on the root
   flips to "true" once the live circuit is connected.

   Human factors: (a) the list is the whole page, so the project is one click away; (b) a member sees only their own
   projects, so nothing else competes for attention; (c) a user without any project is told why the list is empty
   and whom to ask, instead of being shown a blank page.

   The page body is inside SessionGate, which replaces it with a "Session ended" message when the user is no longer
   valid while the page is open. *@
@page "/projects"
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@attribute [Authorize]

<PageTitle>Projects - ReviewCenter</PageTitle>

<SessionGate>
<main class="page" data-testid="projects-page" data-interactive="@InteractiveMarker">
    <div class="page-heading">
        <h1>Projects</h1>
        @if (IsSystemAdmin)
        {
            <a class="action" href="/projects/new" data-testid="new-project-button">+ New project</a>
        }
    </div>
    <p class="page-lead">Choose a project to see its reviews.</p>

    @if (Projects.Count == 0)
    {
        @if (IsSystemAdmin)
        {
            <p class="muted" data-testid="projects-empty">There are no projects yet. Use "+ New project" to create one.</p>
        }
        else
        {
            <p class="muted" data-testid="projects-empty">
                You are not a member of any project yet. Ask an administrator to add you.
            </p>
        }
    }
    else
    {
        <ul class="row-list" data-testid="projects-list">
            @foreach (var project in Projects)
            {
                <li class="row-card" data-testid="project-row-@project.Id">
                    <div class="row-main">
                        <a class="row-title" href="/projects/@project.Id" data-testid="project-link-@project.Id">@project.Name</a>
                        @if (project.Description.Length > 0)
                        {
                            <p class="muted" data-testid="project-description-@project.Id">@project.Description</p>
                        }
                    </div>
                    <span class="row-chevron" aria-hidden="true">›</span>
                </li>
            }
        </ul>
    }
</main>
</SessionGate>
